tonight a las vegas man dealing with  unimaginable grief as he deals with the  loss of three members of his immediate  family to covid19 one after the other he  tells victoria sahil he didn't think the  virus could hit so close to home  victoria joins us live in the newsroom  with really a heartbreaking story  32 year old jason rose has dealt with  more loss in the last week than most  people do in a lifetime he's struggling  to find ways to come to terms with the  loss of his grandfather grandmother and  mother he says it's just a reminder of  how quickly this virus can take away  lives don't be drinking when you are  driving i love you you better take care  jason rose now clings to the voicemails  his mom left him it hasn't even been a  week since she passed of covid my mom  couldn't barely walk like i had to carry  her down the stairs carry into my car  both of rose's grandparents and mom  started showing symptoms of covet 19 two  weeks ago a heart i kind of dropped when  my mom called and said hey we all tested  positive within a week they were in the  hospital together fighting to survive  his grandpa passed away tuesday his  grandmother died thursday then his mom  passed away friday morning just unreal  feeling knowing that  that i saw their faces every single day  and now it's like i wake up and  those faces aren't there you know three  faces gone all three of them were not  vaccinated rose's mom was a high risk  dialysis patient she was worried about  the side effects and his grandparents  relied heavily on their faith could we  have avoided it could we have done this  should we have taken the vaccine  questions rose will never have answered  at this time he and his family are  planning funeral services and also  working on saving their house his mother  bought 22 years ago her dying wish was  to hold on to that house there is a  gofundme to help with the costs that  link will be up on our website at eight  newsnow dot com reporting live from the  newsroom victoria saha 8 news now
 

